{"id":"bela","name":"Bela","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:bela"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Bela","text":"A thing swallowed. (1.) A city on the shore of the Dead Sea, not far from Sodom, called also Zoar. It was the only one of the five cities that was spared at Lot’s intercession (Gen. 19:20, 23). It is first mentioned in Gen. 14:2, 8. (2.) The eldest son of Benjamin (Num. 26:38; “Belah,” Gen. 46:21). (3.) The son of Beor, and a king of Edom (Gen. 36:32, 33; 1 Chr. 1:43). (4.) A son of Azaz (1 Chr. 5:8)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H1106","lemma":"בֶּלַע","xlit":"Belaʻ","gloss":"Bela, the name of a place, also of an Edomite and of two","kjv":"Bela","count":14,"share":1},{"strong":"H788","lemma":"אַשְׁבֵּל","xlit":"ʼAshbêl","gloss":"Ashbel, an Israelite","kjv":"Ashbel","count":3,"share":0.21},{"strong":"H1144","lemma":"בִּנְיָמִין","xlit":"Binyâmîyn","gloss":"Binjamin, youngest son of Jacob","kjv":"Benjamin","count":4,"share":0.29},{"strong":"H1838","lemma":"דִּנְהָבָה","xlit":"Dinhâbâh","gloss":"Dinhabah, an Edomitish town","kjv":"Dinhaban","count":2,"share":0.14},{"strong":"H714","lemma":"אַרְדְּ","xlit":"ʼArd","gloss":"Ard, the name of two Israelites","kjv":"Ard","count":2,"share":0.14},{"strong":"H4427","lemma":"מָלַךְ","xlit":"mâlak","gloss":"to reign","kjv":"consult, indeed, be  king, be  queen","count":4,"share":0.29}],"verses":["Gen.14.2","Gen.14.8","Gen.36.32","Gen.36.33","Gen.46.21","Num.26.38","Num.26.40","1Chr.1.43","1Chr.1.44","1Chr.5.8","1Chr.7.6","1Chr.7.7","1Chr.8.1","1Chr.8.3"],"related":[{"id":"ashbel","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.214,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"aharah","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.2,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"ehud","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.15,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"benjamin","type":"cooccur","shared":5,"jaccard":0.054,"why":"5 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"benjamin-tribe-of",